  "result": "I found the bug and wrote the fix plan, but I haven't changed any code because plan mode is on. I can't call ExitPlanMode here, so approve the plan here and I'll apply it.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` at `src/click/types.py:754` returns `bound - dir`, but the direction is passed the other way round. `convert` calls it with `dir=1` for the min bound and `dir=-1` for the max bound.\n\n**What goes wrong:** this only happens when a bound is open (`min_open=True` or `max_open=True`) together with `clamp=True`.\n- With `min_open=True` and a min of 0, input -5 clamps to -1, which is below the range.\n- With `max_open=True` and a max of 10, input 20 clamps to 11, which is above the range.\n\n**Fix:** change `bound - dir` to `bound + dir`. `FloatRange` isn't affected, since it rejects open bounds when clamping.\n\n**Verification:** I'd add test cases for open-bound clamping in `tests/test_types.py`. Input -5 should give 1 and input 20 should give 9. Then I'd run `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-gentle-quokka.md`.",
